# QuickBuy Project Setup Checklist

Complete step-by-step checklist to get your project up and running.

## ✅ Phase 1: Local Environment Setup (15 minutes)

### 1.1 Install Required Tools

- [ ] **Install Azure CLI**
  ```bash
  # Verify installation
  az --version
  # Should show version 2.50.0 or higher
  ```

- [ ] **Install Terraform**
  ```bash
  # Verify installation
  terraform version
  # Should show Terraform v1.5.0 or higher
  ```

- [ ] **Install Python 3.9+**
  ```bash
  # Verify installation
  python3 --version
  # Should show Python 3.9.x or higher
  ```

- [ ] **Install Git**
  ```bash
  # Verify installation
  git --version
  ```

- [ ] **Install VS Code** (or your preferred IDE)
  - Extensions: Python, Terraform, Azure Account

### 1.2 Configure Azure Access

- [ ] **Login to Azure CLI**
  ```bash
  az login
  ```

- [ ] **Set correct subscription**
  ```bash
  # List subscriptions
  az account list --output table
  
  # Set active subscription
  az account set --subscription "Your Subscription Name"
  
  # Verify
  az account show
  ```

- [ ] **Check your Azure credits/budget**
  - Visit: https://portal.azure.com
  - Check Cost Management + Billing

### 1.3 Create GitHub Repository

- [ ] **Create new repository**
  - Name: `quickbuy-streaming-data-pipeline`
  - Description: "End-to-end real-time data pipeline using Azure Databricks, Event Hubs, and Delta Lake"
  - Visibility: Public (for portfolio)
  - Initialize with README: No (we'll create it)

- [ ] **Clone repository locally**
  ```bash
  git clone https://github.com/yourusername/quickbuy-streaming-data-pipeline.git
  cd quickbuy-streaming-data-pipeline
  ```

## ✅ Phase 2: Project Structure Setup (10 minutes)

### 2.1 Create Folder Structure

- [ ] **Create all directories**
  ```bash
  # Main directories
  mkdir -p azure/terraform/{modules/{storage,eventhubs,keyvault,databricks,monitoring,sql},scripts}
  mkdir -p data_generator
  mkdir -p databricks/{setup,bronze,silver,gold,quality,utilities,workflows}
  mkdir -p tests/{unit,integration,fixtures}
  mkdir -p monitoring/{dashboards,alerts,logs}
  mkdir -p docs/images
  mkdir -p config
  mkdir -p notebooks
  mkdir -p sql
  mkdir -p ci_cd/.github/workflows
  ```

### 2.2 Add Essential Files

- [ ] **Create .gitignore**
  ```bash
  cat > .gitignore << 'EOF'
  # Python
  __pycache__/
  *.py[cod]
  *$py.class
  venv/
  env/
  
  # Terraform
  *.tfstate
  *.tfstate.backup
  .terraform/
  terraform.tfvars
  *.auto.tfvars
  
  # Secrets
  *.env
  secrets/
  *.pem
  *.key
  
  # Data
  data/
  checkpoints/
  *.parquet
  *.delta
  
  # IDE
  .vscode/
  .idea/
  *.swp
  
  # Azure
  *.log
  .databricks/
  EOF
  ```

- [ ] **Create README.md (basic)**
  ```bash
  cat > README.md << 'EOF'
  # QuickBuy Streaming Data Pipeline
  
  Real-time e-commerce analytics pipeline using Azure Databricks, Event Hubs, and Delta Lake.
  
  ## Status: In Development
  
  ## Tech Stack
  - Azure Databricks
  - Azure Event Hubs
  - Delta Lake
  - PySpark
  - Terraform
  
  ## Documentation
  Coming soon...
  EOF
  ```

- [ ] **Initial commit**
  ```bash
  git add .
  git commit -m "Initial project structure"
  git push origin main
  ```

## ✅ Phase 3: Terraform Setup (20 minutes)

### 3.1 Add Terraform Files

- [ ] **Copy all Terraform modules from artifacts**
  - Copy `main.tf` to `azure/terraform/`
  - Copy `variables.tf` to `azure/terraform/`
  - Copy `terraform.tfvars` to `azure/terraform/`
  - Copy each module to `azure/terraform/modules/`
  - Copy `deploy.sh` to `azure/terraform/scripts/`

- [ ] **Update terraform.tfvars**
  ```hcl
  github_username = "your-actual-github-username"
  sql_admin_password = "YourStrongP@ssw0rd123!"  # Change this!
  ```

- [ ] **Make deploy script executable**
  ```bash
  chmod +x azure/terraform/scripts/deploy.sh
  ```

### 3.2 Validate Terraform Configuration

- [ ] **Navigate to Terraform directory**
  ```bash
  cd azure/terraform
  ```

- [ ] **Initialize Terraform**
  ```bash
  terraform init
  ```
  Expected output: "Terraform has been successfully initialized!"

- [ ] **Validate configuration**
  ```bash
  terraform validate
  ```
  Expected output: "Success! The configuration is valid."

- [ ] **Format code**
  ```bash
  terraform fmt -recursive
  ```

## ✅ Phase 4: Deploy Azure Infrastructure (15 minutes)

### 4.1 Pre-Deployment

- [ ] **Review what will be created**
  ```bash
  terraform plan
  ```
  - Review the list of resources
  - Check estimated costs
  - Verify naming conventions

- [ ] **Take a screenshot of the plan**
  - Keep for documentation

### 4.2 Deploy Infrastructure

- [ ] **Run deployment script**
  ```bash
  ./scripts/deploy.sh
  ```
  OR
  ```bash
  terraform apply
  ```

- [ ] **Confirm deployment**
  - Type `yes` when prompted
  - Wait 10-15 minutes for completion

- [ ] **Verify deployment success**
  ```bash
  terraform output
  ```

### 4.3 Post-Deployment Verification

- [ ] **Save deployment outputs**
  ```bash
  terraform output -json > ../../deployment-outputs.json
  ```

- [ ] **Verify in Azure Portal**
  - Go to: https://portal.azure.com
  - Find resource group: `rg-quickbuy-dev-cin`
  - Verify all resources are created

- [ ] **Test access to Databricks**
  ```bash
  # Get URL
  terraform output -raw databricks_workspace_url
  
  # Open in browser and verify you can access it
  ```

- [ ] **Verify Event Hubs**
  ```bash
  EVENTHUBS_NS=$(terraform output -raw eventhubs_namespace_name)
  RG=$(terraform output -raw resource_group_name)
  
  az eventhubs eventhub list --namespace-name $EVENTHUBS_NS --resource-group $RG
  ```

- [ ] **Verify Storage Account**
  ```bash
  STORAGE=$(terraform output -raw storage_account_name)
  
  az storage container list --account-name $STORAGE --auth-mode login
  ```

- [ ] **Verify Key Vault**
  ```bash
  KEY_VAULT=$(terraform output -raw key_vault_name)
  
  az keyvault secret list --vault-name $KEY_VAULT
  ```

## ✅ Phase 5: Data Generator Setup (30 minutes)

### 5.1 Create Data Generator

- [ ] **Copy data generator code from artifacts**
  - Save to `data_generator/ecommerce_generator.py`

- [ ] **Create requirements.txt**
  ```bash
  cat > data_generator/requirements.txt << 'EOF'
  azure-eventhub==5.11.4
  azure-identity==1.13.0
  faker==19.6.2
  python-dotenv==1.0.0
  EOF
  ```

- [ ] **Create virtual environment**
  ```bash
  cd data_generator
  python3 -m venv venv
  source venv/bin/activate  # On Windows: venv\Scripts\activate
  ```

- [ ] **Install dependencies**
  ```bash
  pip install -r requirements.txt
  ```

### 5.2 Create Event Producer

- [ ] **Create event_producer.py**
  ```python
  # We'll create this in the next phase
  # This will send events to Azure Event Hubs
  ```

- [ ] **Create .env file**
  ```bash
  # Get connection strings from Key Vault
  cd ../azure/terraform
  KEY_VAULT=$(terraform output -raw key_vault_name)
  
  # Get secrets
  ORDERS_CONN=$(az keyvault secret show --vault-name $KEY_VAULT --name "eventhub-orders-connection-string" --query value -o tsv)
  CLICKSTREAM_CONN=$(az keyvault secret show --vault-name $KEY_VAULT --name "eventhub-clickstream-connection-string" --query value -o tsv)
  
  # Save to .env
  cd ../../data_generator
  cat > .env << EOF
  EVENTHUB_ORDERS_CONNECTION_STRING="$ORDERS_CONN"
  EVENTHUB_CLICKSTREAM_CONNECTION_STRING="$CLICKSTREAM_CONN"
  EOF
  ```

